1.	10 native English-speaking subjects participated in the English experiments reading 20 articles.
2.	Data has reading times along with various other reading time cognitive measurements for each words.
3.	Data record and creation has been done in two approach each resulting in 200 files.
4.	RT_dataset1P: Data record in the order in which events occurred: Total files= 20*10= 200
5.	RT_dataset2P: Data record in the order in which word occurred i.e., words that are fixated more than once are coded separately. Here again, #files= 20*10= 200
7.	Hence, total files for the English Eye tracking corpus for reading measures= 400

Folders:

per-word-info : Contains word information. The headers discription can be found in Corpus_notes_v2.doc
RT_dataset1P : Type 1 dataset : Description can be found in the Corpus_notes_v2.doc
RT_dataset2P : Type 2 dataset : Description can be found in the Corpus_notes_v2.doc
Sentences : This has simple sentences for the 20 files

per-word-lexical-annotation : Contains dependency information with headers description as below.

Col1 : Word
Col2 : POS tag
Col3 : Itemno		contains the number of the article (1-20) of the Dundee corpus.
Col4 : WNUM		contains a word number that maps to the Dundee Corpus. The Dundee corpus has punctuation and contractions glued to the main word. For this version we separated them but kept the same WNUM for both parts
Col5 : SentenceID	Unique SentenceID within the same Itemno.
Col6 : ID 		Unique word ID within the same SentenceID. This column is referred to in the col DepRel
Col7 : CPOS		Penn Treebank Part-of-speech
Col8 : Head		The ID of the head of this word
Col9 : DepRel		The type of dependency relation to the head

